  "title": "Forest Frontier Commons",
  "rules": [
    "Control any of128 settlers through the same native action interface. The16 pack animals are separate NPC objects.",
    "Walk on grass or trails and cross streams at usable bridges. Grass spends stamina; resting recovers it. Mature tree stage3 blocks passage.",
    "Chop with an axe to obtain timber and open a route. Living cut trees regrow after eligible24-turn periods; bare stumps require replanting.",
    "Mature neighboring woodland supports well recharge. Wells exchange water west-to-east along village rows, so local withdrawals can affect neighbors.",
    "Buckets fill at wells, irrigate crops or extinguish trees. Hoes tend and seed crops. Exchange tools with a waiting neighbor to change work capability.",
    "Shared trails carry loaded pack animals one cell per turn. Trees, broken bridges, other animals and settlers can block them; village docks allow co-location.",
    "Timber and food remain in inventories, stores or moving shipments. Only finite matching trade orders pay shipment commissions.",
    "Dry woodland can ignite and spread fire eastward. Fire consumes trees and damages nearby crops; smoke drains stamina and can injure settlers.",
    "Firebreaks stop growth and fire at that tree site; replanting reverses them. Injured neighbors can be aided with carried food or water.",
    "Work targets the nearest corresponding object within distance one. Clock-rotating actor order resolves contention, then pack movement and ecology run.",
    "Role views show radius-five local entities with declared slot limits. Nearby fire reports can be posted to the neighboring village and become stale.",
    "The896-turn season ends by truncation. This declarative scene is not an executed animation or evidence of learning."
  ],
